{
  "slug": "artel",
  "name": "Artel",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Mesh infrastructure for AI teams. One self-hosted server gives a fleet of agents shared semantic memory, tasks, agent-to-agent messages, and session handoffs. Artel instances mesh together via RSS/JSON feed subscriptions — memory flows across machines, frameworks, and providers with no central coordinator — while a background archivist keeps the shared memory auto-organizing: merging conflicts, synthesizing cross-agent findings, and decaying stale knowledge.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **4 commands**, **5 hooks** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Commands** (4): `artel-handoff` (Save an Artel session handoff so the next session or agent can continue), `artel-recall` (Search Artel shared memory for what the fleet already knows), `artel-remember` (Write a fact, decision, or gotcha to Artel shared memory), `artel-tasks` (Show open Artel tasks, or claim and start the next one)\n- **Hooks** (5): `SessionStart`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `PreToolUse`, `PreCompact`, `Stop`\n- **MCP servers** (1): `artel`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install artel@claude-community` from `NicolasPrimeau/artel`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "hook": 5,
    "command": 4,
    "mcp": 1
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
  "author": {
    "name": "Nicolas Primeau",
    "url": "https://github.com/NicolasPrimeau"
  },
